{#
  hostAliases block that pins every cluster-served LAN name to the ingress VIP, for a pod that
  probes those names from inside the cluster.

  Why a pin at all: a pod without hostAliases resolves through cluster CoreDNS, which forwards
  to resolvers that can answer the public wildcard `*.local.<domain>` with the wrong address.
  The pin keeps a CoreDNS or Pi-hole fault out of the probe path.

  Why one macro: uptime-kuma and blackbox-exporter probe the same ingress names, and both
  Deployments call this, so the two lists cannot drift. Each caller says at its call site why
  that pod probes the ingress. The list is rendered from `containers_list` | lan_hostnames,
  plus the one literal probe host that fronts no workload.

  Emits the `hostAliases:` key at pod-spec indent (6 spaces) and no trailing newline, so a
  caller writes `{{ ingress_host_aliases() }}` on a line of its own. Each item writes its newline
  before itself, for that reason. Import it `with context`: it reads hostvars,
  k8s_primary_node, domain and k3s_metallb_ingress_vip.
#}
{% macro ingress_host_aliases() %}
      hostAliases:
        - ip: "{{ k3s_metallb_ingress_vip }}"
          hostnames:
            # The fleet all-clear tile's probe host (#1342), and the ONLY name here that
            # fronts no workload. It exists so the edge self-check path cannot be outranked:
            # Traefik's router priority is rule length, and an app's Host() rule can be
            # longer than `PathPrefix(`/.well-known/traefik-edge-selfcheck`)` (48 chars) —
            # littlelink's two-host rule is 68 and beat it, measured 2026-09-06, so the tile
            # got littlelink's own 404 body. A name with no IngressRoute anywhere has no
            # Host() router to lose to, whatever gets added later. It is covered by the
            # existing *.local wildcard SAN, so it adds no ACME order.
            # test_the_all_clear_probe_host_fronts_no_route keeps it unrouted.
            - "edge-selfcheck.local.{{ domain }}"
{%- for name in hostvars[k8s_primary_node].containers_list | lan_hostnames %}
{{ "\n" }}            - "{{ name }}.local.{{ domain }}"
{%- endfor %}
{% endmacro %}
